# the developer flags read the real machine, and what they print is the author's
# own configuration; the benign corpus is public content fetched at test time.
# Neither is ever committed. Both default to target/, which is ignored above;
# these names catch a run somebody redirected by hand.
developer-report.txt
*.developer-report.txt
corpus/benign/cache/

# local secrets
.env
*.pem
*.key

# agent worktrees
.claude/worktrees/
